hey everybody what's going on we just  got out of seeing dune here in singapore  it was a media screening i even got the  bracelet on right here and i want to  give you my first impressions of the  movie here i know a lot of you in  america are not going to be able to see  this till october in singapore we are  very fortunate to be one of the few  countries outside the venice film  festival to be able to see it early uh  so big thank you to warner brothers  singapore for that but  i gotta talk about this movie because  this movie surprised me i like denis  villeneuve honestly i like his directing  uh bladerunner 2049 was pretty good but  slow at times prisoners was great you  know and i thought this movie was going  to be a very draggy movie when they told  me the cast i mean it is star studded  from the top to the bottom but when they  mentioned timothy chamelet i was a  little bit like oh really i mean is it  going to work with him  so i went in with sort of mediocre  expectations i'm gonna be honest with  you guys this movie  blew me away it was way above what i  thought it was going to be it's just as  beautiful as the trailers the first  scene comes on you are like okay we are  in a completely different world and one  thing i appreciate about it is is the  trailers give you enough to want to get  you into the movie theaters but once you  sit in  you are just brought into this world  building magnificent cinema masterpiece  from denver new that i think  is gonna get some academy awards now i  don't know if it'll get best film or  best picture but i definitely think  you're gonna get best cinematographer  out of this  art direction uh special effects i mean  score there are so many good things  about this movie so let's talk about the  story for a minute because a lot of  people say based off the book this is an  impossible book to make a movie from  right we saw the 1980s version of dune  it was okay some people loved it some  people just didn't like it at all  this one i have to say i didn't read the  book i don't like reading books before  going to the movie theater because it  will never be the same just won't be but  the world building that they did with  this and the way that they told the  story was very easy to understand you're  really going to get this in the first 15  to 20 minutes of who are the good guys  who are the bad guys what this story is  about on its premise  and then it kind of takes you on that  journey from there  and i mean all the performances are good  i was worried specifically about timothy  chamele's character because you know  when i  saw you know the trailers and i saw paul  there for the first time i'm like going  this guy looks  is he going to just whine and pout the  entire movie is this going to be the  sulkin look you know what i mean but  it's not that paul's journey was  actually one of the more exciting ones  for me and i think denis valeneu did a  fantastic job with that he's not a mary  sue he's not some guy that's able to do  everything and anything right away  um you in some of these movies fall into  that trap based on you know they're  trying to cut time to get to the point  of the film or whatever the case may be  you really get invested in his journey  along the way and it's a uh  you it's i don't want to give away too  much but  it really sets up for a good part two  and i can't wait to see that rebecca  ferguson as his mother  she's a phenomenal actress and this  character has so much more there's so  much underneath you cannot wait to see  what comes out in part two of this film  but it gives you enough to really be  invested with her and she just knocks it  out of the park um oscar isaac as his  father does a fantastic job you see that  bond between father and son you really  believe it and  he's just i love the nuances with him as  well uh jason momoa now usually we're  like yeah i'm jason mamoa man yeah give  me a guinness and he's aquaman  he's toned it down guys he does fit into  this film i was worried about that but  actually he fits into this film really  well as duncan and he's sort of paul's  mentor in this film in terms of you know  combat a little bit in terms of training  in terms of you know uh piloting things  like that he learns a lot of these  things from his mentors and also josh  brolin's character gurney in this so you  get that sense that he's really being  built up to be this leader of course  but  there are some really interesting facets  along the way that make you  think can he be this or some of those  pressures that he feels as a character  i'm talking about paul right now  becoming this person so i love how they  really set up that story in that regard  dave bautista is also really good in  this he doesn't say a lot  but he's very impactful he is a tour de  force on screen with this zendaya was  interesting in this film because we see  her a lot in the trailers  and that's pretty much what you see of  her in the film she's not in it quite a  bit i mean people already said this  already  but she is an integral part of this  movie all the way through and you do  feel the presence all the way in it but  the story is really about paul and his  journey uh in iraqus now in terms of  pacing in this film i was worried it was  going to be kind of long-winded right  because when i saw blade runner 2049  it's a nice looking film but it felt  very long-winded  and it felt draggy at times now there  are some moments in this film that are  slower than others and you know if i was  to look at it from a maybe a critic's  perspective i might say maybe cut off 15  20 minutes out of this film might you  know tighten things up a bit but  one of the things that you get out of  those slower moments are character  building in the moments with some of the  supporting characters or even paul  himself so it was one of those things  where i had to go to the bathroom in the  movie but i didn't know when to go into  the bathroom because every time i want  to go to the bathroom something else  came up and i'm like okay i got to stay  here for this so  if that's the case then the movie's  pacing is pretty good in my personal  opinion based on when i could go to the  bathroom that makes any sense anyway um  i definitely recommend this film and for  you guys in america i know it is opening  up the same day in the theaters as on  hbo max  unless you have a top-tier home theater  system  beautiful screen or projector  fantastic speakers sound proof room  this is  cinematic art and it needs to be seen in  the theaters all right those are my  thoughts on it anyway let me know your  thoughts in the comment section below is  this a film you're excited to see any  questions you have for me i'll try to  answer them without spoiling it for you  with that stay safe take care and i'll  chat in the next one  [Music]  you
 

